From: junkyard
Subject: [PATCH] bms: port to android-mainline

One cumulative patch, kept in two sections: the 6.1 -> 6.18 port this
project first needed for GrapheneOS's 6.18 GKI, then 6.18 -> android-mainline.

== 6.1 -> 6.18 ==
(bms: port to Linux 6.18 (lynx))

Port private/google-modules/bms to the GrapheneOS Linux 6.18 GKI for the gs201 lynx build.
Mechanical API migrations, no intended behaviour change:

  - strlcpy() removed, use strscpy() (6.8)

Files: misc/gvotable.c

lynx-only (kernel/patches-lynx/): felix builds the 6.1 tree these
drivers were written for.

== 6.18 -> android-mainline ==

Linux 6.18 -> android-mainline (7.3):

  * of_node_to_fwnode() -> of_fwnode_handle(); irq_domain_add_linear() ->
    irq_domain_create_linear(of_fwnode_handle(np), ...) (as upstream).
  * alarm_start_relative()/alarm_start() -> alarm_start_timer(.., relative).
  * thermal_of_cooling_device_register() gained a cdev_id argument (0, as
    every in-tree caller passes).
  * misc/logbuffer.c: register_syscore_ops() -> register_syscore() with a
    struct syscore; syscore callbacks take a void *data.
